# Binary files are declared, never auto-detected.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its system gitconfig. 61 of the
# 70 committed PDFs are generated, ASCII-only, and contain no NUL byte, so git
# classified them as TEXT and a fresh checkout rewrote every LF inside them as
# CRLF. The files still opened, pdfplumber read different text, and the
# harness replay missed its cache — on a clean clone, silently.
#
# `binary` = -text -diff -merge: bytes out are exactly the bytes in.

# documents
*.pdf   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.xls   binary
*.docx  binary

# images — the extensions the upload path accepts (_is_image_file), plus site assets
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.tif   binary
*.tiff  binary
*.bmp   binary

# fonts and archives
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.zip   binary
